{
 "id": "surrounded-regions",
 "order": 86,
 "title": "Surrounded Regions",
 "category": "Graphs",
 "difficulty": "Medium",
 "description": "You are given an `m x n` board of `\"X\"` and `\"O\"` characters. A region is a group of `\"O\"` cells connected horizontally or vertically. A region is **surrounded** if none of its cells is on the edge of the board.\n\nCapture every surrounded region by changing its `\"O\"`s to `\"X\"`, **in place**. Your function returns nothing. The tests check `board` afterwards.\n\n**Constraints**\n\n- `1 <= m, n <= 200`",
 "function": "solve",
 "params": [
  "board"
 ],
 "starter": "class Solution:\n    def solve(self, board: List[List[str]]) -> None:\n        pass\n",
 "output_from_arg": "board",
 "hints": [
  "Rather than finding the surrounded regions, find the ones that are **not** surrounded.",
  "A region escapes if it touches the edge. Every `\"O\"` connected to an edge `\"O\"` is safe.",
  "From every edge `\"O\"`, flood-fill and mark the safe cells (for example with `\"T\"`). Then flip every remaining `\"O\"` to `\"X\"` and turn every `\"T\"` back into `\"O\"`."
 ],
